{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00366",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 5.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.53,
      "end_seconds": 8.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.33,
      "end_seconds": 15.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "Okay, um, so I've been feeling faint, and I wanted to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.76,
      "end_seconds": 22.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.28,
      "end_seconds": 25.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Since Monday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.97,
      "end_seconds": 34.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.2,
      "end_seconds": 43.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say. It's every other day. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.22,
      "end_seconds": 46.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.09,
      "end_seconds": 64.87,
      "duration_seconds": 17.78,
      "text": "Well, it usually comes with muscle cramps. Oh, and heavy sweating. As for muscle cramps, about a seven out of ten. It happens a couple of times a week. A pounding headache was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.79,
      "end_seconds": 80.82,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.0,
      "end_seconds": 84.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.98,
      "end_seconds": 88.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any passing no urine or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.23,
      "end_seconds": 93.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "I haven't had passing no urine or fainting, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.21,
      "end_seconds": 98.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any confusion, chest pain, fever or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.11,
      "end_seconds": 101.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.6,
      "end_seconds": 105.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.99,
      "end_seconds": 107.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.75,
      "end_seconds": 110.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.49,
      "end_seconds": 113.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.79,
      "end_seconds": 127.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.27,
      "end_seconds": 132.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Good, you know, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.96,
      "end_seconds": 138.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.73,
      "end_seconds": 143.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "It's amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 143.47,
      "end_seconds": 147.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.58,
      "end_seconds": 152.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.56,
      "end_seconds": 160.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Rosuvastatin. I take it 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.7,
      "end_seconds": 174.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.69,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.88,
      "end_seconds": 177.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Yeah, that's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.3,
      "end_seconds": 179.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.18,
      "end_seconds": 186.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "I mean, uh, I had a lump removed from my back years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.23,
      "end_seconds": 190.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.54,
      "end_seconds": 193.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.44,
      "end_seconds": 198.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.83,
      "end_seconds": 204.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.59,
      "end_seconds": 209.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.92,
      "end_seconds": 210.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.03,
      "end_seconds": 230.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.01,
      "end_seconds": 245.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.25,
      "end_seconds": 253.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high cholesterol. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.41,
      "end_seconds": 266.71,
      "duration_seconds": 12.3,
      "text": "Uh, not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 267.21,
      "end_seconds": 274.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 97 over 56, respiratory rate 16, temperature is 37.1 degrees, heart rate 108."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.13,
      "end_seconds": 278.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Alright, how's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.36,
      "end_seconds": 284.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.53,
      "end_seconds": 290.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.46,
      "end_seconds": 293.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.99,
      "end_seconds": 307.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Capillary refill is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.6,
      "end_seconds": 309.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.84,
      "end_seconds": 321.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Your skin is warm and a bit clammy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.9,
      "end_seconds": 333.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.54,
      "end_seconds": 337.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.25,
      "end_seconds": 339.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.88,
      "end_seconds": 369.22,
      "duration_seconds": 14.34,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is heat exhaustion with some dehydration. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out an electrolyte imbalance yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.59,
      "end_seconds": 372.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Hmm, should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.13,
      "end_seconds": 388.61,
      "duration_seconds": 15.48,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now heat exhaustion with some dehydration is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling faint, since Monday, severe, and no passing no urine or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.03,
      "end_seconds": 391.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Right, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.52,
      "end_seconds": 395.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.63,
      "end_seconds": 396.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.62,
      "end_seconds": 420.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. We should do blood salts for dehydration. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use ORS, 1 sachet, three times a day, for two days. That should help with dehydration."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.75,
      "end_seconds": 423.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.25,
      "end_seconds": 429.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Avoid the midday sun for a few days and keep a water bottle with you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.4,
      "end_seconds": 448.52,
      "duration_seconds": 19.12,
      "text": "Okay. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.68,
      "end_seconds": 450.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.55,
      "end_seconds": 461.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you become confused or stop sweating, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 463.15,
      "end_seconds": 463.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.6,
      "end_seconds": 472.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Please come and see me in three days. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.3,
      "end_seconds": 477.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "So, um, I come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 479.18,
      "end_seconds": 483.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 484.86,
      "end_seconds": 487.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Uh, no questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 487.62,
      "end_seconds": 488.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}